  "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x)$, we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n{log}_{2}\u2061(4-2x)+1=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}\u2061(4-2x)+1 & =0 \\\\ {log}_{2}\u2061(4-2x) & =-1 \\\\ {2}^{{log}_{2}\u2061(4-2x)} & ={2}^{-1} \\\\ 4-2x & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -2x & =-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{7}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=\\frac{7}{4}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
